## What I did

Eliminated an exact 5-line duplicated block that was copy-pasted into **12 result-view classes** in `core/src/main/java/com/taobao/arthas/core/command/view/`. Every view that supports classloader matching reproduced the same "Matched classloaders" rendering logic:

```java
if (result.getMatchedClassLoaders() != null) {
    process.write("Matched classloaders: \n");
    ClassLoaderView.drawClassLoaders(process, result.getMatchedClassLoaders(), false);
    process.write("\n");
    return;
}
```

**Change:** I added a single static helper where `drawClassLoaders(...)` already lives, in `ClassLoaderView`:

```java
public static boolean drawMatchedClassLoaders(CommandProcess process, Collection<ClassLoaderVO> matchedClassLoaders) {
    if (matchedClassLoaders == null) {
        return false;
    }
    process.write("Matched classloaders: \n");
    drawClassLoaders(process, matchedClassLoaders, false);
    process.write("\n");
    return true;
}
```

Each call site collapses to:

```java
if (ClassLoaderView.drawMatchedClassLoaders(process, result.getMatchedClassLoaders())) {
    return;
}
```

This is behavior-preserving (the helper returns whether it drew anything — true exactly when the collection was non-null — so the early `return` fires under the identical condition as before). It respects the existing Command → Model → View layering and the shared-renderer seam the code already used (`ClassLoaderView.drawClassLoaders`). The models don't share a common getter interface, so passing the collection in is the clean way to unify them without a riskier model-hierarchy change. Net: −48/+27 lines, output rendering unchanged.

## Verification

- `./mvnw -pl core -am test-compile -o` — compiles cleanly.
- `./mvnw -pl core -o test -Dtest=ClassLoaderViewTest` — **7/7 pass, BUILD SUCCESS**.
- `git diff --check` — clean, no whitespace errors.

